# Enterprise workforce identity (MEDUI.D4A.4.0W)

```
ONE ENTERPRISE WORKFORCE IDENTITY
 → MANY FACILITY ASSIGNMENTS
 → PRECISE PROFESSION
 → DERIVED SYSTEM ROLE
 → DEPARTMENT / SERVICE ROUTING
 → CAPABILITY-GATED DOCUMENTATION
```

## Separate concepts (never collapse)

| Concept | Meaning |
|---|---|
| **Profession** | What the employee is (`UserRole.professionCode`) |
| **System role** | Broad `RoleCode` family (ADMIN, PROVIDER, RN, …) |
| **Department / service line** | Where they work |
| **Specialty** | Clinical specialization — **not** `DepartmentCode` |
| **Capability** | What they may perform |
| **Credential** | License / NPI / attribution identity |

## Hard prohibitions

- No `DentistUser` / `TherapistUser` / parallel employee registries
- No duplicate provider identity system
- No RoleCode explosion (`MD_ROLE`, `DO_ROLE`, `NP_ROLE`, …) unless an audit proves an existing authority requires it
- No UI-only profession list (SSoT: `enterpriseWorkforceProfessionD4c11.ts`)
- No service-line-specific employee registry
- No provider authority inferred from department alone
- No department/module access inferred from `RoleCode.PROVIDER` alone (e.g. Clinic physician ≠ Dental)

## Provider family

`PHYSICIAN_MD` / `PHYSICIAN_DO` / `RESIDENT_PHYSICIAN` / `PHYSICIAN_ASSISTANT` / `NURSE_PRACTITIONER` / legacy `MEDICINE` all derive **systemRole = PROVIDER** while retaining precise profession for attribution, signing labels, credentialing, billing, and supervision.

Never invent MD vs DO vs NP vs PA from bare `RoleCode.PROVIDER`.

## Access intersection

```
FACILITY MEMBERSHIP
 ∩ ENABLED SERVICE LINE
 ∩ DEPARTMENT / ASSIGNMENT
 ∩ ROLE
 ∩ PROFESSION
 ∩ CAPABILITY
```

Facility ADMIN clinical override remains governed by D5A.5C. Platform `MEDORA_SUPER_ADMIN` alone is not facility clinical membership.
